  "notes": "A formal word used when two things correspond or align. Common in academic, legal, and business writing. In everyday conversation, {合|あ}う or {一致|いっち}する are more natural.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {意見|いけん}が{合致|がっち}する: opinions agree\n- {条件|じょうけん}に{合致|がっち}する: to match conditions\n- {方針|ほうしん}と{合致|がっち}する: to be in line with policy\n- {目的|もくてき}に{合致|がっち}する: to match the objective\n- {基準|きじゅん}に{合致|がっち}する: to meet standards\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {一致|いっち}する: to match, to agree — more common, nearly synonymous\n- {合|あ}う: to match, to fit — everyday word\n- {該当|がいとう}する: to correspond to, to apply — focuses on meeting criteria\n- {適合|てきごう}する: to conform to — more technical, often for standards compliance",
